[{"id":"reg-predict-load","itemId":"register-enable","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"At a rising edge where <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> is 1, <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>; at the other edges it keeps its value. All four bits work the same way, so only bit 0 is drawn: <code class=\"nobreak\">d[0]</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code>. Cycles 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> is 1 at the edges that start cycles 3, 5 and 7, so <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d[0]</code> there: 0, 1 and 0. At every other edge <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> keeps its value, even where <code class=\"nobreak\">d[0]</code> differs: in cycle 4 <code class=\"nobreak\">d[0]</code> is 1 but <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> stays 0, and in cycle 6 <code class=\"nobreak\">d[0]</code> is 0 but <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> stays 1.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"reg-en-hold","source":"hdl/level-02/reg_en/reg_en_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"reg_en_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"load","path":"reg_en_tb.load","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[2.5,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4.5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6.5,"1"]]},{"label":"d[0]","path":"reg_en_tb.d0","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1.5,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3.5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[7.5,"1"]]},{"label":"q[0]","path":"reg_en_tb.q0","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[3,"0"],[5,"1"],[7,"0"]],"samples":["1","1","1","0","0","1","1","0"]}]},"answer":"q[0]","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"reg-report-luts","itemId":"register-enable","role":"core","promptHtml":"Vivado built <code class=\"nobreak\">reg_en.sv</code>, the 4-bit register with <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code>, for the Arty A7-100T. Below is the Slice Logic table of its Utilization report. A slice is one of the small groups of LUTs and flip-flops the chip is built from, so the Slice LUTs row counts LUTs; Used is how many this design takes.","explanationHtml":"<p>Read the Used column of the Slice LUTs row. Each FDRE has a clock enable, CE, and a reset input, R, so Vivado joins <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> straight to them and needs no logic for either (lesson 2.4). The Slice Registers row below counts the flip-flops, one for each bit of <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code>.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/reg_en/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":32,"excerpt":["+-------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+","|        Site Type        | Used | Fixed | Prohibited | Available | Util% |","+-------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+","| Slice LUTs              |    0 |     0 |          0 |     63400 |  0.00 |","|   LUT as Logic          |    0 |     0 |          0 |     63400 |  0.00 |","|   LUT as Memory         |    0 |     0 |          0 |     19000 |  0.00 |","| Slice Registers         |    4 |     0 |          0 |    126800 | <0.01 |","|   Register as Flip Flop |    4 |     0 |          0 |    126800 | <0.01 |","|   Register as Latch     |    0 |     0 |          0 |    126800 |  0.00 |","| F7 Muxes                |    0 |     0 |          0 |     31700 |  0.00 |","| F8 Muxes                |    0 |     0 |          0 |     15850 |  0.00 |","| Unique Control Sets     |    1 |       |          0 |     15850 | <0.01 |","+-------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+"],"ask":"How many LUTs did Vivado use for reg_en?","answer":"0","numeric":true},{"id":"reg-predict-reset-wins","itemId":"register-enable","role":"core","promptHtml":"This is lesson 2.4's <code class=\"nobreak\">reg_en</code>, with its reset in use: at some edges <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> are both 1. All four bits work the same way, so only bit 0 is drawn: <code class=\"nobreak\">d[0]</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code>. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> for every cycle.","explanationHtml":"<p>The block tests <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> first (lesson 2.4). At the edges that start cycles 1 and 4, <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> are both 1, and <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> becomes 0 although <code class=\"nobreak\">d[0]</code> is 1: the reset wins. At the edge that starts cycle 5 the reset clears it again. Where <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> is 0, <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d[0]</code> only at edges with <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> at 1 (cycles 0, 3, 6 and 7), and keeps its value in cycle 2.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"reg-en-reset-wins","source":"hdl/level-02/reg_en/reg_en_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"reg_en_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"rst","path":"reg_en_tb.rst","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[0.5,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[3.5,"1"],[5.5,"0"]]},{"label":"load","path":"reg_en_tb.load","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2.5,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5.5,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"d[0]","path":"reg_en_tb.d0","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[6.5,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"q[0]","path":"reg_en_tb.q0","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1,"0"],[3,"1"],[4,"0"],[7,"1"]],"samples":["1","0","0","1","0","0","0","1"]}]},"answer":"q[0]"},{"id":"reg-find-bug","itemId":"register-enable","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"This register should take <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> only at rising edges where <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> is 1, and keep its value at the others. Verilator warns that <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> is never used. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p>The <code class=\"nobreak\">else</code> line gives <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> the value of <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> at every edge where <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> is 0, whether <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> is 1 or not, so <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> does nothing. Verilator reports the problem where <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> is declared, the port line, but that line is not the mistake: deleting the port would silence the warning and leave a register that never keeps its value. Written <code>else if (load) q &lt;= d;</code>, the line uses <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> as the comment says.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-02/reg_en_bug/reg_en_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// A 4-bit register. At a rising edge: rst clears it; otherwise, if load","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// is 1, it takes d; otherwise it keeps its value.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"reg_en_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"       clk,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"       rst,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"       load,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"3","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] d,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"3","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] q","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"if","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" (rst) q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"4'd0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"else","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"     q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]],"bugLine":12,"fixLine":"else if (load) q <= d;"},{"id":"reg-fill-load","itemId":"register-enable","role":"core","promptHtml":"Type what goes before <code>q &lt;= d;</code> so that the register takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> only at edges where <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> is 1, and the reset still wins.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>else if (load)</code> runs only when <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> is 0 and <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> is 1. At edges where <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> is 0, no line gives <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> a value, so the flip-flops keep theirs (lesson 2.4). The <code class=\"nobreak\">else</code> ties the line to the reset's <code class=\"nobreak\">if</code>, so at an edge where both are 1, only the reset line runs.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-02/reg_en/reg_en.sv","firstLine":1,"totalLines":14,"before":["// A 4-bit register. At a rising edge: rst clears it; otherwise, if load","// is 1, it takes d; otherwise it keeps its value.","module reg_en (","  input  logic       clk,","  input  logic       rst,","  input  logic       load,","  input  logic [3:0] d,","  output logic [3:0] q",");","  always_ff @(posedge clk) begin","    if (rst)       q <= 4'd0;"],"blankLine":{"left":"    ","right":" q <= d;"},"after":["  end","endmodule"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"// A 4-bit register. At a rising edge: rst clears it; otherwise, if load","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// is 1, it takes d; otherwise it keeps its value.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"reg_en","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"       clk,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"       rst,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"       load,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"3","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] d,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"3","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] q","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"if","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" (rst)       q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"4'd0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":" q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]},"after":[[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]]},"accept":["else if (load)","else if(load)"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"The missing condition"},{"id":"reg-report-fdre","itemId":"register-enable","role":"core","promptHtml":"Vivado built <code class=\"nobreak\">reg_en.sv</code>, the 4-bit register with <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code>, for the Arty A7-100T. Below is the Primitives table of its Utilization report: one row for each kind of cell, with how many the design uses.","explanationHtml":"<p>Read the FDRE row. <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> has four bits, and a register has one flip-flop for each bit (lesson 2.4). <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> add no cell of their own: they go to each FDRE's CE and R inputs. IBUF and OBUF are the pins, and BUFG is the clock.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/reg_en/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":179,"excerpt":["8. Primitives","-------------","","+----------+------+---------------------+","| Ref Name | Used | Functional Category |","+----------+------+---------------------+","| IBUF     |    7 |                  IO |","| OBUF     |    4 |                  IO |","| FDRE     |    4 |        Flop & Latch |","| BUFG     |    1 |               Clock |","+----------+------+---------------------+"],"ask":"How many FDRE flip-flops did Vivado use for reg_en?","answer":"4","numeric":true},{"id":"reg-predict-pair","itemId":"register-enable","role":"core","promptHtml":"In <code class=\"nobreak\">load_pair</code>, one <code class=\"nobreak\">always_ff</code> block holds two lines inside <code>if (load)</code>: the line for <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>, and the line for <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code>, both with <code class=\"nobreak\">&lt;=</code>. <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> is not drawn. Just before the window's first edge, <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> are both 0. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> for every cycle.","explanationHtml":"<p>Work out <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> alongside <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code>. At an edge where <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> is 1, <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> takes the value <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> had before that edge (lesson 2.2). At an edge where <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> is 0, no line gives either a value, so both keep theirs (lesson 2.4). So <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> is 1, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0 and <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> is 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0. In cycle 2, <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> is 0: <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> keeps its 1 and does not take <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code>'s 0; in cycle 3 it takes the 0 that <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> kept. If your <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> copied <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> at each load, you read the two lines one after the other, like software.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"load-pair","source":"hdl/level-02/load_pair/load_pair_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"load_pair_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"load","path":"load_pair_tb.load","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2.5,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5.5,"1"]]},{"label":"d","path":"load_pair_tb.d","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1.5,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[7.5,"1"]]},{"label":"q2","path":"load_pair_tb.q2","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[3,"0"],[4,"1"],[7,"0"]],"samples":["0","1","1","0","1","1","1","0"]}]},"answer":"q2"}]